expensive:
And earnestly watered the potted plants;
She didn't dismember expensive toys;
And never would play with the little boys.

expectation:
Their faith the everlasting troth;
Their expectation fair;
The needle to the north degree

explaining:
Like messengers that mock the message’ mien,
Explaining all but the explanation;
As if we a ciphered letter’s cipher hit

expecting:
And praise my Lady's kindness,
Expecting me to speak;
I like the proud ones best

expansive:
Case I 'd allus pictered great folks
On a mo' expansive plan;
But I t'ought I could respect him

expresses:
‘And yet to mean so well, and fail so foul,
Expresses ne’er another beast than man;
The antithesis is human. Harken, dear;

expands:
Become divine i’ the utterance! while for him
The poet, the speaker, he expands with joy;
The palpitating angel in his flesh

expectant:
And angels open their bright ranks for thee;
For thee they wait, and with expectant eye
Thy spouse leans downward from th' empyreal sky:

expir'd:
Soon as appear'd the Goddess long desir'd,
Sick at the view, she languish'd and expir'd;
Thus from the splendors of the morning light

expiration:
Has strangled that habitual breath of home
Whose expiration leaves all houses dead;
And wheresoe'er I look is hideous change.
